  "projects": {
    "2016": [
      {
        "title": "Easier Project Model Management",
        "short_description": "The main objective of this project is to enhance the flexibility and versatility of Sigmah software to meet new requirements and satisfy user...",
        "description": "<p>The main objective of this project is to enhance the flexibility and versatility of Sigmah software to meet new requirements and satisfy user feedback and will be working in this regard as the GSoC project. The Sigmah's concept is extremely fascinating and  can be worked over so that it accomplishes greater heights.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Nikita",
        "code_url": "https://github.com/niksj/GsocWork/blob/master/README.md",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2016/projects/6500037328633856/"
      }
    ],
    "2017": [
      {
        "title": "Easier project model management",
        "short_description": "Most appealing for me: Project idea#2: Easier project model management.\nI am already familiar with customer requirements related to the idea. The...",
        "description": "<p>Most appealing for me: Project idea#2: Easier project model management.\nI am already familiar with customer requirements related to the idea. The idea is interested for me and I have practical experience and knowledge to implement the requirements. So I’ve applied fix for issue #1046 as well as I’ve also implemented on my local development environment fix for issue #1058 . During testing of implemented solution I discovered that related to the fixed issue functionality also can be improved. \nDetailed calendar plan is described in my Project proposal document.</p>\n<p>Equally interesting for me: idea 1: Full-featured calendars\nI am familiar with customer requirements  and I know how to implement some of them, other ideas also very interesting for me but require additional investigation to find solution (like an idea #824 Calendars export to other devices.</p>\n<p>Less interesting for me :  idea 3: Search\nI know how to implement #536 Dashboard project table extra searchable columns.\nAs for second requirement: #535 Full text search engine – this is very interesting task cause it is require a knowledge and experience with  Apache Solr.\nNevertheless I am ready to take the challenge.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "ALIAKSEI KARPAU",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/Seal98/1c8c9285c56cce0583f6484987136cfd",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2017/projects/5758848111476736/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Full-text search of database text and files, enforcing ACLs and search contexts.",
        "short_description": "Sigmah has a lot of database text content that can be indexed and searched by keywords, providing a useful capability to users to fetch the actual...",
        "description": "<p>Sigmah has a lot of database text content that can be indexed and searched by keywords, providing a useful capability to users to fetch the actual entities (orgunits, projects) that correspond to such keywords.</p>\n<p>Users also upload files (Word, PDF, others) that have a lot of text. Here the search results may point to both the files themselves, and also to the entities owning those files where the search term was found.</p>\n<p>Entity access (view) permissions have to be enforced in both cases. Another challenge is to integrate both database search and file search under the same UI, provide users with helpful search features (similar terms, relevance rankings).</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Aditya Adhikary",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/indianauthority97/56c713f3e51741e206a865f1a996d4f6",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2017/projects/5763644784640000/"
      }
    ]
  },
